{%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
  <style>
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
      {%- unless section.settings.allow_transparent_header -%}
        margin-block-start: calc(var(--section-vertical-spacing) / 2);
      {%- endunless -%}
      --slideshow-top-gap: {% unless section.settings.allow_transparent_header %}calc(var(--section-vertical-spacing) / 2){% else %}0px{% endunless %};
      margin-block-end: var(--section-vertical-spacing);
      {%- if section.settings.transition_type != 'fade' -%}
        --slideshow-background: {{ section.settings.background.rgb }};
      {%- endif -%}
    }

    {%- comment -%}
    First section on the page, right under the site header: the gap above the slideshow is the page's side margin (--container-gutter), the same as every
    other first section (theme.css), instead of half of the section spacing. The min-height below subtracts the same value (--slideshow-top-gap), so the slideshow
    still fills the screen. With the transparent header there is no gap and nothing changes.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- unless section.settings.allow_transparent_header -%}
      main > #shopify-section-{{ section.id }}:first-child {
        margin-block-start: var(--container-gutter);
        --slideshow-top-gap: var(--container-gutter);
      }
    {%- endunless -%}

    {%- if section.settings.floating_slideshow -%}
      {%- comment -%}
      The page's side gutter (the .container margin) sits on the section wrapper itself, outside the section, instead of on the
      slideshow inside it: the editor's outline then spans only the slideshow, which still respects the page's side padding.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
        margin-inline: max(var(--container-gutter), 50% - var(--container-max-width) / 2);
      }

      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow-wrapper {
        margin-inline: 0;
      }
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.border_radius == 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
      theme.css gives .slideshow a mask-image, a trick to make overflow: hidden follow rounded corners in Safari. With square corners it
      does nothing visible, but a mask forces the browser to composite and repaint the whole slideshow, videos included, on every frame -
      a known cause of choppy video. Only kept when the corners are rounded.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow {
        -webkit-mask-image: none;
        mask-image: none;
      }
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.hide_header_logo -%}
      {%- comment -%}
      "Hide the header logo": whenever this slideshow is on the page, the logo in the header is not shown, in any header state (transparent over
      the slideshow, solid, scrolled, floating or not). It is only made invisible and unclickable - not removed - so the header's layout
      (menu centering, icons) stays exactly where it is and screen readers still get the store name.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      .header__logo {
        opacity: 0 !important;
        pointer-events: none !important;
      }
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.blur_intensity > 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
      Blur only (the same backdrop blur the pop-ups and the newsletter use), with no color: a layer over each IMAGE slide's picture (video slides are left alone),
      under the text, so the text stays sharp. It covers the whole slide and never blocks clicks or swipes.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__blur {
        position: absolute;
        inset: 0;
        grid-area: auto;
        -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur({{ section.settings.blur_intensity }}px);
        backdrop-filter: blur({{ section.settings.blur_intensity }}px);
        pointer-events: none;
      }
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
    Logo on an image slide (snippets/slideshow-logo.liquid), centered over the picture and under the slide's text. Its box is absolutely
    positioned: it fills the slide (so the logo is centered on the slide itself) but takes no part in the slide's layout, so the image's own
    size can never widen the slide. grid-area: auto matters: the content box gives every direct child the grid-area of its inner area
    (theme.css), and an absolute child of a grid is sized against its grid area. It is a flex box with the inner padding (container gutter
    + 0.5rem, the same as the slide's text) and the image has to fit inside what is left. Never blocks clicks or swipes.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__logo {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      grid-area: auto;
      box-sizing: border-box;
      padding: calc(var(--container-gutter) + 0.5rem);
      pointer-events: none;
      justify-content: center;
      align-items: center;
      display: flex;
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__logo img {
      flex: 0 1 auto;
      width: min(var(--slideshow-logo-width), 100%);
      height: auto;
      max-height: 100%;
      min-width: 0;
      min-height: 0;
      object-fit: contain;
    }

    @media screen and (min-width: 700px) {
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__logo img {
        width: min(var(--slideshow-logo-width-desktop), 100%);
      }
    }

    {%- comment -%}Full size (after the rules above, so it wins at every width): fills the box inside the padding, fitted without cutting or stretching.{%- endcomment -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__logo--full img {
      flex: 1 1 auto;
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      max-height: none;
    }

    {%- comment -%}
    The text's distance from the slide's edges is the same inner padding as the floating containers (container gutter + 0.5rem,
    see faq.liquid / reviews.liquid), at every width. .content-box
    (theme.css) is shared with many other sections, so its own value (the larger of 1.5rem and the gutter, shrinking
    in narrow containers) stays as is and is only overridden here; the section id in the selector beats those
    container-width rules.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__slide .content-box {
      --content-box-spacing: calc(var(--container-gutter) + 0.5rem);
    }

    {%- comment -%}
    A heading with its decorative icon is a full-width row (title on one side, the icon on the other), so inside a
    centered or end-aligned slide the title would stay at the start while the rest of the text follows the slide.
    Shrinking the row to its content lets the prose rules (margin-inline: auto on its children) place it like any
    other text block.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__slide .prose > .heading-icon-row {
      width: fit-content;
    }

    {%- comment -%}
    Matches the existing .min-h-fill convention (assets/theme.css): subtract the sticky header/
    announcement bar area from the svh height, since that's real occupied space above the fold on
    every page except when this section is both first AND allows a transparent header - there, the
    header floats over the slideshow instead of pushing it down, so only the (non-transparent)
    announcement bar/countdown still needs subtracting.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__slide .content-box {
      min-height: calc({{ section.settings.mobile_height }}svh - var(--sticky-area-height, 0px) - var(--slideshow-top-gap, 0px));
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }}:first-child [allow-transparent-header] .slideshow__slide .content-box {
      min-height: calc({{ section.settings.mobile_height }}svh - var(--announcement-bar-height, 0px) - var(--announcement-bar-gap, 0px) - var(--header-top-gap, 0px) - var(--countdown-condensed-height, 0px));
    }

    @media screen and (min-width: 700px) {
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__slide .content-box {
        min-height: calc({{ section.settings.desktop_height }}svh - var(--sticky-area-height, 0px) - var(--slideshow-top-gap, 0px));
      }

      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }}:first-child [allow-transparent-header] .slideshow__slide .content-box {
        min-height: calc({{ section.settings.desktop_height }}svh - var(--announcement-bar-height, 0px) - var(--announcement-bar-gap, 0px) - var(--header-top-gap, 0px) - var(--countdown-condensed-height, 0px));
      }
    }
  </style>

  <div class="slideshow-wrapper {% if section.settings.floating_slideshow %}container{% endif %}">
    <slideshow-carousel id="slideshow-{{ section.id }}" allow-swipe cell-selector=".slideshow__slide" {% if section.settings.allow_transparent_header %}allow-transparent-header{% endif %} class="slideshow" transition="{{ section.settings.transition_type }}" {% if section.settings.autoplay %}autoplay="{{ section.settings.cycle_speed }}" {% if section.settings.pause_auto_rotate_on_hover %}pause-on-hover{% endif %}{% endif %} style="border-radius: {{ section.settings.border_radius }}px;" role="region" aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="{{ 'general.accessibility.slideshow' | t | escape }}">
      {%- content_for 'blocks' -%}

      {%- if section.blocks.size > 1 -%}
        {%- content_for 'block', type: '_slideshow-controls', id: 'slideshow-controls' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </slideshow-carousel>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.slideshow.name",
  "class": "shopify-section--slideshow",
  "tag": "section",
  "max_blocks": 5,
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": [
      "header",
      "custom.overlay"
    ]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "allow_transparent_header",
      "label": "t:global.section.allow_transparent_header",
      "info": "t:global.section.allow_transparent_header_info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "floating_slideshow",
      "label": "Floating",
      "info": "Activado: el slideshow respeta los márgenes laterales de la página y el marco del editor se ajusta solo a él. Desactivado: va de borde a borde de la pantalla.",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_radius",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "t:sections.slideshow.border_radius",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "blur_intensity",
      "label": "Blur (image slides)",
      "info": "Blurs the picture of every image slide, without adding any color. The text stays sharp. Video slides are not blurred. 0 turns it off.",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 10
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Header logo"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "hide_header_logo",
      "label": "Hide the header logo",
      "info": "Hides the logo at the top of the header whenever this slideshow is on the page, whether the header is transparent or not.",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "mobile_height",
      "label": "t:sections.slideshow.mobile_height",
      "min": 30,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "desktop_height",
      "label": "t:sections.slideshow.desktop_height",
      "min": 30,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "transition_type",
      "label": "t:sections.slideshow.transition_type",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "fade",
          "label": "t:sections.slideshow.transition_type_options.fade"
        },
        {
          "value": "vertical_reveal",
          "label": "t:sections.slideshow.transition_type_options.vertical_reveal"
        },
        {
          "value": "curtain",
          "label": "t:sections.slideshow.transition_type_options.curtain"
        },
        {
          "value": "distortion",
          "label": "t:sections.slideshow.transition_type_options.distortion"
        },
        {
          "value": "perspective",
          "label": "t:sections.slideshow.transition_type_options.perspective"
        },
        {
          "value": "scale_down",
          "label": "t:sections.slideshow.transition_type_options.scale_down"
        }
      ],
      "default": "curtain"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "autoplay",
      "label": "t:sections.slideshow.auto_rotate_between_slides",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "pause_auto_rotate_on_hover",
      "label": "t:sections.slideshow.pause_auto_rotate_on_hover",
      "default": false,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.autoplay }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "cycle_speed",
      "min": 4,
      "max": 20,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "sec",
      "label": "t:sections.slideshow.cycle_speed",
      "default": 6,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.autoplay }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "background",
      "label": "t:global.colors.background",
      "info": "t:sections.slideshow.background_info",
      "default": "#000000"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "_slideshow-image-slide"
    },
    {
      "type": "_slideshow-video-slide"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:sections.slideshow.name",
      "category": "t:global.categories.banners",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "_slideshow-controls",
          "id": "slideshow-controls",
          "static": true
        },
        {
          "type": "_slideshow-image-slide",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "settings": {
                "text": "Slide 1",
                "heading_size": "h1"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "_slideshow-image-slide",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "settings": {
                "text": "Slide 2",
                "heading_size": "h1"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
